# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: `type=` is MANDATORY on `fragment`, and the twelve
# values are UML's `InteractionOperatorKind` taken whole. The clause number in
# both diagnostics is §17.12.15.3 — NOT §17.6.2, which is Abstract Syntax and
# is registered as a FALSE citation in spec/standards-claims.tsv (S024).
#
# The missing-key case and the wrong-value case are different mistakes and get
# different sentences: the first says why there is no default (UML has one and
# FigDown declines it), the second just lists the twelve.
#
# `operand` needs `in=` for the same kind of reason and is pinned in the same
# file: a compartment with no fragment is not a smaller thing, it is nothing.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
lifeline s "S"
fragment a "no operator at all"
fragment b "not one of the twelve" type=maybe
fragment d "the enum is bare, not quoted" type="alt"
operand o "no fragment"
